  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q71-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve $\\log_2(x)+\\log_2(x-3)-\\log_2(x+2)=2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=8$.\n\nUse the product and quotient laws; the original domain $x>3$ excludes the other root, $-1$.",
      "worked": "The original arguments require $x>0$, $x-3>0$ and $x+2>0$, hence $x>3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2\\left(\\frac{x(x-3)}{x+2}\\right)&=2\\\\\\frac{x(x-3)}{x+2}&=4\\\\x^2-3x&=4x+8\\\\x^2-7x-8&=0\\\\(x-8)(x+1)&=0\\\\x&=8\\text{ or }x=-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nOnly $x=8$ satisfies $x>3$, so the solution is $x=8$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 70
  },
